<title>BELGIUM: EU's deSilguy sees 13 states meeting EMU target.</title>
<headline>EU's deSilguy sees 13 states meeting EMU target.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European monetary affairs commissioner Yves Thibault de Silguy on Wednesday said 13 European Union countries would meet the deficit target for monetary union in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Thirteen member states will meet the reference value,&quot; de Silguy told a committee of the European Parliament, a reference to the three percent-GDP-ratio included in the Maastricht Treaty.</p>
<p>He also predicted that a majority of countries would join monetary union in 1999.</p>
<p>The Commission's twice-yearly economic forecasts showed only Italy and Greece failing to bring their deficits down to Maastricht's target in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6838</p>
</text>
